※ pl4g-test: compile=error
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4622 LANG_CONTAINER_OWNER_UNKNOWN

※ Writing an element needs to know which allocator the container keeps its elements in: what goes
※ in is kept there, as it is or copied, and a container of `⎕heap`'s gives back what it replaces.
※ The compiler knows that of a container this body made, or was handed by name -- not of one
※ reached through a field.

type Holder = names: str⟦2⟧

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u6:
    let h: mut Holder = Holder(.names ← ⟦"a", "b"⟧)
    h.names⟦0⟧ ← "c"
    0u6
